    "answer": "hesitation/bewilderment/perplexity/doubt/indecision | illusion/delusion | inability-to-reach-enlightenment",
    "mnemonic": "Remember how you learned that <ja>迷う</ja> means \"to go astray\" or \"to get lost?\" Well when you feel like you're about to go astray or get lost it causes <vocabulary>hesitation</vocabulary>. You end up with a lot of <vocabulary>doubt</vocabulary> about where to go or what to do. It's a natural progression.",
